---
title: OnboardHQ — Role-Based Workflow
---
sequenceDiagram
  accTitle: Four simulated role swimlanes
  accDescr: HR initiates onboarding, while document collection, IT provisioning and team tasks proceed in parallel. Documents and task completion remain separate measures.
  autonumber
  participant hr as HR
  participant emp as Employee
  participant it as IT Admin
  participant mgr as Manager
  Note over hr,mgr: Demo role switcher in one browser, no authentication or messages sent between real users
  rect rgb(238, 242, 255)
    hr->>hr: Create employee and select onboarding type
    hr->>hr: Create seven-item document checklist
    hr->>hr: Initiate journey, generate four role-owned tasks
    Note over hr,mgr: Documents exist before initiation, branches can progress independently
  end
  par Document collection and review
    hr-->>emp: Required / optional checklist shown in profile
    loop Missing or rejected items
      emp->>emp: Pick PDF/JPG/PNG or sample metadata
      alt Invalid name, MIME, empty file or size above 10 MB
        emp->>emp: Show validation error, no submission saved
      else Valid metadata only
        emp-->>hr: Save versioned metadata as Pending Review
        alt Verify
          hr->>hr: Mark Verified, remarks optional
        else Reject
          hr-->>emp: Mark Rejected with required remarks
          emp->>emp: Resubmit replacement metadata
        else Request resubmission
          hr-->>emp: Mark Missing with required remarks
          emp->>emp: Submit next version
        else Waive
          hr->>hr: Mark Waived with required remarks
        end
      end
    end
    hr->>hr: Review separate mandatory document readiness
  and Employee checklist
    emp->>emp: Update own Employee-owned task status
    emp->>emp: Complete or reopen assigned tasks
  and Equipment and application access
    it->>it: Create inventory, assign available equipment
    alt Equipment already assigned to another employee
      it->>it: Reject reassignment, unassign first
    else Equipment available
      it-->>emp: Display assigned laptop / accessory
    end
    emp-->>it: Create Pending access request for self
    Note over hr,mgr: All demo roles may create Pending requests, only IT Admin decides
    alt Approve
      it-->>emp: Approved access status
      it->>it: Revoke if needed, reopen to Pending
    else Reject
      it-->>emp: Rejected access status
      it->>it: Reopen to Pending if needed
    end
    it->>it: Complete or reopen IT-owned tasks
  and HR and Manager checklist
    hr->>hr: Add / edit tasks, set owner, due date and priority
    mgr->>mgr: Manage Manager-owned tasks and team introduction
    alt Task blocked
      mgr->>mgr: Save required reason, resolve and update status
    else Work finished
      mgr->>mgr: Complete task, reopen if needed
    end
    hr->>hr: Complete HR tasks, HR can manage any task
  end
  rect rgb(236, 253, 245)
    hr->>hr: Inspect Dashboard / Reports and readiness measures
    Note over hr,mgr: Journey becomes Completed when all its tasks are Completed
    Note over hr,mgr: Documents and provisioning do not automatically gate that status
  end
